          "slice": "InFlightSubmissionReassessed",
          "description": "S0.4/S0.5's sharpest open question, generalized: what happens to a submission already in-flight when the rules it's being evaluated against change underneath it. Leaning toward re-evaluation as the safer default for a governance-critical system, but this is a business decision (policyApplied), not an architecture default. Revocation (S0.5) pushes for the stricter, immediate interpretation given it correlates with higher-risk situations; routine revisions (S0.4) may be more relaxed (checked at next decision point).",
